          "funFact": "Did you know? There are many types of {name}, like romaine and iceberg! Lettuce was eaten by ancient kings. It grows from tiny seeds in rows.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and rustle your hands like salad leaves!"
        },
        "cucumber": {
          "about": "A {name} is a long cool green vegetable with lots of water inside. It is crunchy and mild, great in salads and raita. {name} grows on a vine in gardens.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? {name} slices can cool tired eyes in stories and spa tricks! Pickles are often made from cucumbers. They grow very fast in summer.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and make a cool “ahhh” face like a refreshing bite!"
        },
        "corn": {
          "about": "{name} has sweet yellow kernels on a cob and grows on tall stalks in fields. It can be boiled, grilled, or popped into popcorn. {name} is a grain that people eat as a vegetable.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? Each {name} kernel is a seed! Popcorn pops when the water inside heats up. Corn plants can grow taller than you.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and pretend to twist an imaginary corn cob!"
        },
        "pumpkin": {
          "about": "A {name} is a big orange vegetable with thick flesh and many seeds inside. It is used in pies, soups, and Halloween lanterns. {name} grows on a vine along the ground.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? Giant {name}s can weigh hundreds of kilograms in contests! Pumpkin seeds are tasty when roasted. Native people used pumpkins for food long ago.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and carve a happy face in the air!"
        },
        "eggplant": {
          "about": "An {name} is a shiny purple vegetable with soft flesh used in curries and grilled dishes. It grows on a bush-like plant with pretty leaves. {name} soaks up flavors when it cooks.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? {name} can also be white or striped, not only purple! It is called brinjal in India. Eggplants love warm sunny weather.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and rub your hands on a smooth purple surface!"
        },
        "mushroom": {
          "about": "A {name} is not a plant but a fungus that grows in damp places and forests. It comes in many shapes and colors, like button, portobello, and shiitake. {name} adds a savory taste to pizza and soups.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? Some {name}s glow in the dark! Never eat wild mushrooms without an expert — some are poisonous. Mushrooms grow very fast overnight.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and pop up from a squat like a mushroom!"
        },
        "chili": {
          "about": "A {name} is a small hot pepper that can be red or green and makes food spicy. The heat comes from capsaicin inside. {name} is used carefully in curries and sauces.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? Birds can eat hot {name}s without feeling the burn! Milk helps cool your mouth if it is too spicy. Chili plants love warm weather.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and fan your tongue after one tiny pretend bite!"
        },
        "tomato": {
          "about": "A {name} is a red juicy fruit that we often use like a vegetable in salads, ketchup, and sauce. It grows on a vine and ripens in the sun. {name} is full of vitamins and lycopene.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? Botanically a {name} is a fruit, not a vegetable! Tomato plants can grow very tall with support. Ketchup is made from millions of tomatoes.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and roll your hands like a round tomato!"
        },
        "peanut": {
          "about": "A {name} is not a nut but a legume that grows underground in shells. It is crunchy and full of protein and healthy fats. {name} is used to make peanut butter and snacks.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? {name} plants flower above ground but the peanuts form below! George Washington Carver found many uses for peanuts. Peanut butter sandwiches are popular worldwide.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and spread your palms like peanut butter on bread!"
        },
        "sweetPotato": {
          "about": "A {name} has orange sweet flesh and grows underground like a potato but tastes sweeter. It is baked, mashed, or made into fries. {name} has vitamins that help your body grow.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? {name} leaves are also edible in some places! They are popular in many countries at holiday meals. Orange color comes from beta-carotene like carrots.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and hug a warm imaginary baked sweet potato!"
        }
      }
    },
    "flowers": {
