      "tractor": "Works on the farm",
      "airplane": "Flies in the sky",
      "helicopter": "Flies up high",
      "boat": "Floats on water",
      "ship": "Big boat on the sea",
      "taxi": "Takes you places",
      "policeCar": "Keeps people safe",
      "scooter": "Small two-wheel ride",
      "metro": "City train underground",
      "rocket": "Flies to space"
    },
    "detail": {
      "aboutTemplate": "A {name} is a vehicle that helps people or things move from one place to another. Learning vehicle words helps children understand roads, travel, and safety rules in everyday life.",
      "funFactTemplate": "Did you know? Some vehicles roll on wheels, some float on water, and some fly in the sky! Each vehicle is designed for a special kind of travel.",
      "tryTemplate": "Say \"{name}\" slowly three times. Then act it out with your hands or body and tell a grown-up where you usually see this vehicle.",
      "aboutWithSubtitle": "A {name} is a vehicle that {subtitle}.",
      "car": {
        "about": "A car is a small road vehicle with four wheels. Families use cars to visit school, markets, parks, and relatives. Seat belts help everyone stay safe while the car is moving.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Modern cars have lights, mirrors, and brakes that help drivers see and stop safely. Electric cars can run with batteries instead of fuel.",
        "try": "Pretend your hands are on a steering wheel. Turn left, turn right, and say \"{name}!\""
      },
      "bus": {
        "about": "A bus is a big vehicle that carries many people at once. School buses and city buses help families travel together and reduce traffic on roads.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Some buses have special ramps so everyone can get in more easily. In some cities, double-decker buses have two levels of seats.",
        "try": "Line up your toys like bus passengers. Say \"{name}!\" and pretend to ring the stop bell."
      },
      "taxi": {
        "about": "A taxi is a car you can hire to go from one place to another. A driver takes you where you ask, and families pay a fare at the end of the ride.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Taxis can be different colors in different cities. Phone apps can help adults book taxis quickly and safely.",
        "try": "Wave your hand like calling a taxi and say \"{name}!\" Then politely say, \"Please take me home.\""
      },
      "policeCar": {
        "about": "A police car helps police officers protect people and keep roads safe. Officers use police cars to reach places quickly during emergencies.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Police cars have flashing lights and sirens so other vehicles know to give way. These signals are only for urgent situations.",
        "try": "Blink your fingers like flashing lights and say \"{name}!\" Practice standing safely at the side of a road."
      },
      "scooter": {
        "about": "A scooter is a small two-wheel vehicle. Some scooters are kicked by foot, and others have motors. They are useful for short trips in busy areas.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Helmets protect your head while riding scooters. Riding slowly near people keeps everyone safer.",
        "try": "Take one pretend kick forward and say \"{name}!\" Then pretend to wear a helmet before riding."
      },
      "bicycle": {
        "about": "A bicycle has two wheels, pedals, and handlebars. Children and adults ride bicycles for fun, exercise, and short travel.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Bicycles do not need fuel, so they are eco-friendly. Reflectors and lights help riders stay visible.",
        "try": "Move your legs in the air like pedaling and say \"{name}!\" Count 1 to 5 like slow pedal turns."
      },
      "motorcycle": {
        "about": "A motorcycle is a fast two-wheel motor vehicle. It can move quickly on roads, so riders need balance, attention, and proper safety gear.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Helmets, jackets, and gloves help protect motorcycle riders. Some motorcycles are used by delivery workers and police teams.",
        "try": "Pretend to wear a helmet, hold handlebars, and say \"{name}!\" in a gentle voice."
      },
      "truck": {
        "about": "A truck is a strong vehicle that carries heavy goods like food boxes, furniture, and building materials. Trucks help shops and homes get important supplies.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Some trucks have very long trailers for big loads. Delivery trucks bring many of the things we use every day.",
        "try": "Pretend to lift a heavy box and load it into a truck. Say \"{name}!\" and make a soft beep-beep sound."
      },
      "fireTruck": {
        "about": "A fire truck carries firefighters, water hoses, and ladders to emergency places. Firefighters use these tools to control fires and help people stay safe.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Fire trucks are usually bright red so people can spot them quickly. Their ladders can reach high floors of buildings.",
        "try": "Say \"{name}!\" and pretend to hold a hose with both hands. Then practice a quiet siren sound."
      },
      "ambulance": {
        "about": "An ambulance is an emergency vehicle that takes sick or injured people to hospitals quickly. Medical helpers inside give first aid while traveling.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Ambulances use lights and sirens to move through traffic faster. Other vehicles should make space when an ambulance passes.",
        "try": "Put one hand on your heart, take a calm breath, and say \"{name}!\" Then say, \"Please make way.\""
      },
      "train": {
        "about": "A train runs on metal tracks and can carry many people or goods in connected coaches. Trains are useful for long-distance and city travel.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Some trains are very fast, while others carry heavy cargo. Train stations help people move safely from one city to another.",
        "try": "Move your arms like train rods and say \"{name}!\" Count how many imaginary coaches your train has."
      },
      "metro": {
        "about": "A metro is a city train, often underground or on raised tracks. Metros help people avoid road traffic and reach places on time.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Metro trains stop at many stations, and doors open automatically. Many people use metros daily for school and work.",
        "try": "Stand still and pretend to hold a metro pole. Sway gently and say \"{name}!\""
      },
      "tractor": {
        "about": "A tractor is a powerful farm vehicle used to plow fields and pull tools. Farmers use tractors to prepare land and grow crops we eat.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Tractors move slowly but can pull very heavy equipment. Different tractor tools help with sowing, watering, and harvesting.",
        "try": "Walk slowly with strong steps like a tractor and say \"{name}!\""
      },
      "airplane": {
        "about": "An airplane flies high in the sky using wings and engines. Airplanes help people travel between faraway cities and countries much faster than roads.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Pilots and cabin crew train carefully for safe flights. Airplanes can fly above clouds where the sky looks bright and wide.",
        "try": "Spread your arms like wings, glide in place, and say \"{name}!\""
      },
      "helicopter": {
        "about": "A helicopter has spinning blades on top that let it lift straight up and hover. Helicopters can land in small places where big planes cannot.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Helicopters help in rescue missions, medical transport, and news reporting. Their spinning rotors create the loud chop-chop sound.",
        "try": "Spin one finger above your head like a rotor and say \"{name}!\" softly."
      },
      "rocket": {
        "about": "A rocket is a powerful vehicle that travels into space. Rockets carry satellites, science tools, and sometimes astronauts beyond Earth.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Rockets need huge force to escape Earth's gravity. Space missions help us learn about planets, weather, and stars.",
        "try": "Count down with a grown-up: 3, 2, 1... Say \"{name}!\" and do one careful jump."
      },
      "boat": {
        "about": "A boat is a water vehicle that floats on rivers, lakes, or near the shore. Some boats use oars, while others use sails or motors.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Boats float because their shape pushes water aside. Life jackets are important safety gear when riding boats.",
        "try": "Sit and rock gently side to side like small waves, then say \"{name}!\""
      },
      "ship": {
        "about": "A ship is a very large water vehicle built for seas and oceans. Ships carry passengers, cars, food, and containers across long distances.",
        "funFact": "Did you know? Cargo ships move many products between countries. Some ships are taller than buildings and have giant engines.",
        "try": "Wave like a sailor and say \"{name}!\" Then pretend to spot land with your hand above your eyes."
      }
    }
  },
